1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,143
Orchard Core reads the translations of its interface from PO files.

2
00:00:05,143 --> 00:00:09,456
In this video you install the community French files, enable them on a

3
00:00:09,456 --> 00:00:13,940
site, see where PO files are read from, and write PO entries of your own.

4
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:23,325
A PO file, short for Portable Object, is a plain text file with

5
00:00:23,325 --> 00:00:26,169
one entry for each translated text.

6
00:00:26,169 --> 00:00:31,301
An entry holds a context in msgctxt, the original text in msgid, and

7
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:33,520
its translation in msgstr.

8
00:00:34,270 --> 00:00:38,001
The name of the file, or of its folder, is the culture:

9
00:00:38,001 --> 00:00:42,160
a language such as fr, or a language and region such as fr-CA.

10
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:46,747
Orchard Core loads the files of the culture of the request, and shows

11
00:00:46,747 --> 00:00:49,560
the original text without a translation.

12
00:00:53,760 --> 00:01:00,137
The community translates Orchard Core on Crowdin, and anyone can add a language or improve one.

13
00:01:00,137 --> 00:01:06,829
In the Orchard Core project, select French, then Download or Upload, and then Download translations.

14
00:01:06,829 --> 00:01:09,860
The browser saves a zip file named fr.zip.

15
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:17,484
Create a folder named Localization in the root of your site, and extract fr.zip into it.

16
00:01:17,484 --> 00:01:22,750
The result is a folder named fr, with one PO file for each module.

17
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:28,396
The CMS application targets publish the Localization folder with the site.

18
00:01:28,396 --> 00:01:32,740
Other projects include the folder as content in the project file.

19
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:38,125
With Docker, keep PO files in Localization, not App_Data, because a volume mounted

20
00:01:38,125 --> 00:01:41,430
on App_Data hides the files it already contains.

21
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:49,040
To use the files, enable the Localization feature.

22
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:52,797
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for Localization.

23
00:01:53,249 --> 00:01:57,233
Localization is listed under the Internationalization category.

24
00:01:57,233 --> 00:01:59,369
Let's select its Enable button.

25
00:01:59,826 --> 00:02:03,681
The feature adds a Localization group to the Settings menu.

26
00:02:03,681 --> 00:02:06,646
Let's open Settings, Localization, Cultures.

27
00:02:07,098 --> 00:02:09,814
The table lists the cultures of the site.

28
00:02:09,814 --> 00:02:14,438
Let's choose French in the list, select Add culture, and then select Save.

29
00:02:14,889 --> 00:02:18,249
Saving restarts the site, and a notice confirms it:

30
00:02:18,249 --> 00:02:22,139
The site has been restarted for the settings to take effect.

31
00:02:26,339 --> 00:02:30,582
To test a culture, add ?culture=fr to the address of a page.

32
00:02:30,582 --> 00:02:35,081
The culture has to be one of the supported cultures of the site.

33
00:02:35,081 --> 00:02:37,909
Let's open the Features page this way.

34
00:02:39,503 --> 00:02:43,642
This recording uses a small French file with entries for a few texts

35
00:02:43,642 --> 00:02:45,152
of the Features page.

36
00:02:45,152 --> 00:02:49,683
The title, the search box, the Bulk Actions button, the Enable buttons, and

37
00:02:49,683 --> 00:02:52,033
the count of features are in French.

38
00:02:52,695 --> 00:02:56,355
The menu on the left stays in English, because the file has no

39
00:02:56,355 --> 00:02:57,754
entry for its texts.

40
00:02:57,754 --> 00:03:01,575
Orchard Core shows the original text for a text without an entry.

41
00:03:02,028 --> 00:03:08,248
A browser configured with French as its language gets the same translations, without the query string.

42
00:03:12,448 --> 00:03:17,176
Orchard Core searches several places for a file named after the culture:

43
00:03:17,176 --> 00:03:21,721
the Localization folder of each module and theme, of the site, and of

44
00:03:21,721 --> 00:03:26,388
each tenant, a separate site in the application, under App_Data, Sites.

45
00:03:27,138 --> 00:03:29,579
Files can also be split by module.

46
00:03:29,579 --> 00:03:35,559
The community download uses a folder named after the culture, with one file for each module.

47
00:03:35,559 --> 00:03:38,488
A folder named after the module works too.

48
00:03:39,238 --> 00:03:42,249
All the files found for a culture are merged.

49
00:03:42,249 --> 00:03:46,383
When two files define the same entry, the later one wins, in the

50
00:03:46,383 --> 00:03:47,859
order of this list.

51
00:03:47,859 --> 00:03:53,468
The culture folder loads last, so its entries replace those of the site and tenant files.

52
00:03:54,218 --> 00:03:57,502
A file serves only the culture in its path.

53
00:03:57,502 --> 00:04:02,662
For a regional culture such as fr-CA, write fr-CA files, or select Fall

54
00:04:02,662 --> 00:04:08,358
back to parent culture(s), so that missing texts are looked up in the fr files.

55
00:04:12,558 --> 00:04:18,133
In a file such as Localization/fr.po, you write entries for your own texts.

56
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:22,607
For a service, the context is the full name of the type the

57
00:04:22,607 --> 00:04:26,668
localizer is created for, here MyNamespace.MyService.

58
00:04:27,418 --> 00:04:31,915
For a view, the context is the path of the view, starting at

59
00:04:31,915 --> 00:04:36,071
the module folder, with dots and without the extension.

60
00:04:36,071 --> 00:04:40,908
The Features page uses OrchardCore.Features.Views.Admin.Features.

61
00:04:41,658 --> 00:04:46,754
An entry without a context applies wherever a text has no entry of its own context:

62
00:04:46,754 --> 00:04:52,021
Orchard Core looks for the entry with the context first, and then for the one without.

63
00:04:52,021 --> 00:04:54,998
An entry with an empty translation is ignored.

64
00:04:55,748 --> 00:05:00,067
To translate a single tenant, put the file in the Localization folder of

65
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:02,336
that tenant, under App_Data, Sites.

66
00:05:02,336 --> 00:05:04,496
The other tenants do not read it.

67
00:05:04,496 --> 00:05:08,814
Its entries are merged with the other files, and the culture folder wins

68
00:05:08,814 --> 00:05:10,198
for the same entry.

69
00:05:10,948 --> 00:05:15,380
Keep the numbered placeholders of the original text in the translation.

70
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:21,308
After you edit a PO file, restart the application, because translations are loaded once and kept.

71
00:05:21,308 --> 00:05:23,668
Plural forms have a separate video.

72
00:05:25,668 --> 00:05:29,503
PO files are plain text named after a culture, so you install the

73
00:05:29,503 --> 00:05:33,608
community files, add your own entries for the texts they do not cover,

74
00:05:33,608 --> 00:05:35,444
and restart the application.

75
00:05:35,444 --> 00:05:36,848
Thanks for watching.

